        <mxCell id="step-1-badge-legend" value="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="102" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-1-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;The way in · in progress&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;A tenant is its subdomain. Without a domain, {tenant}.&amp;lt;NLB IP, dashed&amp;gt;.sslip.io resolves to the load balancer itself. The page is on port 80, the API on 8000 of the same host.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="100" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-2-badge-legend" value="2" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="252" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-2-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;One NLB, two ports · in progress&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;The AWS Load Balancer Controller (branch infra/edge) makes one internet-facing NLB with IP targets that keeps the client's address: 80 to the web app, 8000 to Kong. Not yet run on AWS.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="250" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-3-badge-legend" value="3" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="402" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-3-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Kong routes by path&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;Kong (DB-less) clears every tenant header a client sends, sets X-Tenant-Slug from the subdomain, checks JWT signatures on six routes, counts a per-IP rate limit in Redis and routes each path to its service, with retries off.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="400" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-4-badge-legend" value="4" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="552" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-4-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Each service owns its store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;Six services each own a Postgres database, with its own roles, under forced row-level security. Live fans out over Redis Pub/Sub, Search queries OpenSearch, Analytics reads ClickHouse, Notification sends through Mailpit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="550" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-5-badge-legend" value="5" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="702" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-5-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Outbox, relays, Kafka&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;A write and its outbox row commit in one transaction. Four relays claim rows in order (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED), Avro-encode them against Schema Registry and publish. Live sends live.interactions straight to Kafka, as JSON.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="700" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-6-badge-legend" value="6" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="852" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-6-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Consumers build read models&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;The search indexer, the ticketing projection, analytics-ingest, Notification's email dispatch and Community's feed fan-out each read their topics into a store of their own.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="850" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-7-badge-legend" value="7" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="1002" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-7-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;GitOps from main&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;On every commit to main, publish.yml pushes the app and web images to GHCR, tagged with the commit. Argo CD syncs main through a read-only deploy key and runs exactly those images.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="1000" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-8-badge-legend" value="8" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="1152" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-8-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Terraform stops at the cluster&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;bootstrap/ (kept): the S3 state bucket and a $10 monthly budget. envs/demo (torn down after each window): VPC with one NAT, EKS with KMS-encrypted Secrets, the node group, ECR, Pod Identity roles and the EBS CSI driver. infra/eks/up.mjs installs the stores, setup and charts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="1150" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-9-badge-legend" value="9" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#007CBD;strokeColor=default;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=22;labelBackgroundColor=none;fontFamily=Helvetica;shadow=1;glass=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2650" y="1302" width="40" height="38" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-9-desc-legend" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;A real domain · planned&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0,0,0), rgb(255,255,255));&quot;&gt;Not chosen yet. An ACM certificate for it puts TLS on 443 and 8000 at the NLB, and the services switch to production because the address is https.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2702" y="1300" width="388" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
